================================================================================
WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
================================================================================

This repository is a fork and does not hold copyright in everything it
contains. The licence above is the fork's grant over the fork's own work. It
cannot and does not relicense anyone else's.

Read this section together with THIRD-PARTY.md, which carries the attribution
that must accompany any redistribution, and docs/LICENSING.md, which sets out
the evidence and the reasoning in full.


1. COVERED BY THE LICENCE ABOVE

   Work originated in this fork: the installer (install/), the platform layer
   and the clean-room console wrappers (platform/), the test suite (tests/),
   the tooling (tools/), the documentation (docs/, README.md, SECURITY.md,
   THIRD-PARTY.md, this file), and the fork's modifications to inherited files.


2. INHERITED UNDER BSD-3-CLAUSE FROM UNetLab / EVE-NG

   130 files carry an intact BSD-3-Clause notice from Andrea Dainese and Alain
   Degreffe: 111 device templates under templates/, 16 files under includes/,
   and 3 under themes/default/js/. A further 9 files are the same lineage and
   had their notice restored by this fork after it was found to have been
   removed upstream.

   Those notices are the grant. Do not remove them. THIRD-PARTY.md reproduces
   the notice in full, which is what condition 2 above asks of a binary
   redistribution.

   This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or a product of UNetLab
   Ltd or EVE-NG Ltd.


3. INHERITED FROM PNETLab WITH NO LICENCE GRANT AT ALL

   A substantial part of this tree originates in pnetlab/pnetlab_main, which
   was published publicly with no LICENSE file and reports no licence. That
   includes the device driver layer under devices/, the Laravel application
   under store/app/, and the React frontend source under store/resources/.

   No licence has been granted for that code by its author, and this fork
   cannot grant one on its author's behalf. The licence above does not extend
   to it. Anyone relying on this repository should read docs/LICENSING.md
   section 2.3, which states the position, the evidence, and its limits
   plainly.


4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS UNDER THEIR OWN TERMS

   Bundled libraries, fonts and assets keep their own licences: Slim (MIT),
   Parsedown (MIT), Ace (BSD-3-Clause), jQuery, Bootstrap, jsPlumb and others
   (MIT), the Ubuntu font family (Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0), DejaVu (Bitstream
   Vera / public domain amendment), Apache Guacamole (Apache-2.0). Each is
   listed in THIRD-PARTY.md.

   One of them is copyleft and it matters: CKEditor 5 is licensed
   GPL-2.0-or-later, and it is compiled into the frontend build output that
   this repository commits under store/public/react/ and vendors~. .
   Those built files are a combined work and carry GPL-2.0-or-later terms. The
   licence above does not apply to them. See docs/LICENSING.md section 2.4.
